Acting Spokesperson
New York, New York
April 29, 2025
AS DELIVERED
At the outset, I wish to thank Under-Secretary-General Fleming for her leadership of the Department of Global Communications. I also want to congratulate you, Chair, on your election, and thank the former Committee Chair.
I’d like to outline some of the principles that will guide the United States’ participation in this year’s committee:
First, the United States is making every effort to protect freedom of expression and will not tolerate efforts to trample freedom of expression at home or abroad. Government censorship of speech is intolerable in a free society. We will not shy away from calling out countries imposing censorship tactics, such as government-imposed shutdowns of the Internet and undue restrictions on freedom of expression online.
For example, as the Government of Iran stifles the free flow of information to the Iranian people, the United States remains committed to supporting Internet freedom and the right of all Iranians to freedom of expression.
We call on all other member states to strengthen the free flow of information.
The United States will continue to call out those countries and individuals blocking access to information or deliberately undermining local trust in the UN, in particular by promoting narratives that threaten peacekeeper safety and security. We urge all member states to do the same. We reject attacks on the credibility of UN peacekeeping missions.
Similarly, this committee must remain vigilant against insidious attempts to inject political or ideological language into its work, including language which undermines respect for human rights.
Moreover, we do not support the promulgation of soft global governance that is inconsistent with U.S. sovereignty and adverse to the rights and interests of Americans, such as 2030 Agenda and the SDGs.
As a general principle, the United States is reaffirming the foundational principle of sovereignty in foreign affairs. Our primary responsibility is to our citizens — to meet their needs, ensure their safety, preserve their rights, and defend our values — and our approach is shaped by this commitment.
Thank you.
