UNITED STATES MISSION TO THE UNITED NATIONS
Office of Press and Public Diplomacy
FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE
April 8, 2025
Readout of Chargé d ’Affaires Dorothy Shea’s Meeting with October 7 Hostage Families
The below is attributable to United States Mission to the United Nations Acting Spokesperson Saul Mercado:
Ambassador Dorothy Shea, Acting Representative of the United States to the United Nations, met today with families of those taken hostage by Hamas on October 7. Ambassador Shea commended the family members for their commitment to reminding the world of the plight of their loved ones and all hostages abducted by Hamas. President Trump has been clear: all of the remaining 59 hostages must be immediately released. The Ambassador also conveyed the United States’ deep concern for the mental and physical health of the hostages and emphasized the need to return those who are still living, as well as those who have been murdered by Hamas in captivity. President Trump, along with Special Envoy to the Middle East Steve Witkoff, are working diligently to secure the immediate release of all hostages. The United States will continue pressing partners at the UN to add their voice and effort to bring them home now.
