Ambassador Dorothy Shea
Chargé d’Affaires ad interim
New York, New York
April 4, 2025
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Chair. And thank you other honored Permanent Representatives, Deputy Permanent Representatives, and others who came out for this important meeting, which we thank you for organizing. And thank you to the briefers also for your presentations today. We agree on the need to harness trustworthy artificial intelligence for the maintenance of international peace and security.
Colleagues, at the AI Action Summit in Paris earlier this year, U.S. Vice President JD Vance outlined the tremendous opportunities AI presents and noted that the United States is focusing on AI’s opportunities. The AI revolution will enhance the UN Security Council’s ability to maintain international peace and security.
As the world’s leader on AI, the United States supports systems that are free from ideological bias and open to everyone. The United States wants to embark on the AI revolution with a spirit of openness and collaboration.
We believe AI will revolutionize economic innovation, national security, free expression, and countless other fields. Restricting AI development would paralyze one of the most promising technologies seen in generations, while handing the initiative to nefarious actors who are unburdened by any such restraints.
Colleagues, AI has the potential to play a transformative role in the maintenance of international peace and security. AI can facilitate better, faster decision making, which will help militaries avoid unintended engagements and also enhance states’ ability to implement their obligations under International Humanitarian Law.
The United States encourages UN peacekeeping missions to utilize technology to protect civilians, including by bolstering early warning, promoting information integrity, and countering actions that undermine the ability of UN missions to implement their mandates.
AI can enhance the timeliness of life-saving information necessary to counter threats to humanitarian operations, and mitigate interruptions to food deliveries, protect humanitarian personnel, and counter restrictions on free expression.
Colleagues, it is important to ensure AI is not misused by malicious actors to facilitate human rights abuses, as well as by leveraging AI to improve civilian protection, address inappropriate suppression of information, and enhance lifesaving humanitarian response amid conflicts.
We have seen – and we continue to see – hostile foreign adversaries weaponize AI software to rewrite history, surveil users, and censor speech. This is hardly new, of course. As they do with other tech, some authoritarian regimes have misused AI to strengthen their militaries, their intelligence, and surveillance capabilities; capture foreign data; and create propaganda and disinformation to undermine other nations’ national security.
This only underscores the importance of the theme of this event about leveraging AI for the maintenance of international peace and security. And so, we thank you again for this effort.
Thank you, Chair.
